{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For managing acid reflux, focus on foods that are naturally low in fat and acid, and high in fiber. Here’s a concise guide to what works best:\n\n**Top Food Choices for Acid Reflux Relief**\n\n- **Vegetables:** Broccoli, leafy greens, cucumbers, asparagus, carrots, beetroot, celery, lettuce, sweet peppers, kale, spinach, and brussels sprouts. These are low in fat and acid, making them gentle on your stomach.\n- **Whole Grains:** Oatmeal, brown rice, barley, jowar, and whole grain breads. Their high fiber content helps absorb stomach acid and reduce symptoms.\n- **Lean Proteins:** Skinless chicken, turkey, fish (especially oily fish like salmon and tuna), seafood, tofu, and egg whites. Avoid frying; opt for baking, broiling, or grilling.\n- **Non-Citrus Fruits:** Bananas and melons are especially good—they’re alkaline and can soothe the esophagus.\n- **Soothing Drinks:** Ginger tea, unsweetened coconut water, cold milk, and buttermilk can help neutralize acid and calm symptoms.\n- **Healthy Fats:** Walnuts, flaxseed, olive oil, and avocados are better choices than saturated fats.\n\n**Foods to Avoid:** Citrus fruits, high-fat meats, fried foods, and anything spicy or acidic.\n\n**Personalized Tip:** If you prefer Indian foods, include barley, jowar, wheat, cumin, coriander, and cardamom. Cold milk is also recommended.\n\nWould you like meal ideas or a sample daily menu tailored to your preferences?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0044-72-05971:1": -0.014883078634738922, "clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:2": -0.01717234030365944, "clueweb22-en0035-60-12129:5": -0.019477417692542076, "clueweb22-en0010-33-07725:0": -0.020598655566573143, "clueweb22-en0024-83-01996:17": -0.021400606259703636}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I eat dinner late at night.", "I want to increase my protein intake.", "I like a variety of fruits."]}], "references