{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Here’s a concise guide to the main types of coffee and what shapes their taste, so you can find one you’ll enjoy:\n\n**1. Bean Type**\n- **Arabica:** Most popular, smoother, less bitter, often with mild and complex flavors. Generally preferred for quality and flavor.\n- **Robusta:** Stronger, more bitter, higher caffeine. Used in many commercial blends; less nuanced flavor.\n\n**2. Origin**\n- **Central & South America:** Clean, sweet, balanced. Good if you want a classic, approachable taste.\n- **Africa:** Complex, often fruity or floral. Try these if you like adventurous, layered flavors.\n- **Asia:** Earthy, sometimes spicy or herbal. Good for those who prefer a deeper, richer cup.\n\n**3. Roast Level**\n- **Light Roast:** Brighter, more acidic, highlights bean’s origin flavors.\n- **Medium Roast:** Balanced, slightly sweet, less acidity.\n- **Dark Roast:** Bold, smoky, bitter notes dominate; origin flavors are muted.\n\n**4. Processing Method**\n- **Washed (Wet):** Cleaner, brighter flavors.\n- **Natural (Dry):** Fruitier, heavier body.\n\n**5. Blends vs. Single Origin**\n- **Single Origin:** Distinct, bold flavors from one place.\n- **Blends:** More balanced, smooth, and consistent.\n\n**Personalized Tip:** Since you dislike sourness, avoid light roasts and many African beans. Try medium or dark roasts from Central or South America, or blends featuring Arabica beans.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific brands or brewing methods to match your taste?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0016-20-09441:8": -0.015236065723001957, "clueweb22-en0027-09-07083:10": -0.022065723314881325, "clueweb22-en0016-20-09441:9": -0.023836590349674225, "clueweb22-en0010-28-18869:13": -0.024051444604992867, "clueweb22-en0024-99-03258:4": -0.02700965665280819}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I want to lose weight.", "I get grumpy if I don