{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-2_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For a regional oaked Chardonnay with hazelnut notes—matching your taste and your location in Canada—here’s what you need to know:\n\n**Best Regional Oaked Chardonnays for Hazelnut Lovers**\n\n- **Burgundy, France:** The gold standard for oaked Chardonnay, especially from Puligny-Montrachet in Burgundy. These wines are renowned for their rich, buttery texture and layered flavors of hazelnut, vanilla, and honey. If you want the classic experience, look for “White Burgundy” or “Puligny-Montrachet” at your local wine shop.\n- **Sonoma County & Napa (California):** Russian River Valley and Los Carneros produce world-class oaked Chardonnays with pronounced hazelnut, butterscotch, and caramel notes. These are widely available in Canada and often offer a slightly riper, fruitier profile than Burgundy.\n- **Ontario (Canada):** The Niagara Peninsula and Prince Edward County are emerging as top regions for Chardonnay. Local producers are increasingly using oak aging to create Chardonnays with creamy, nutty, and toasty flavors—sometimes with a distinct hazelnut note. These wines are fresher and more affordable than imports, and you’ll be supporting Canadian vineyards.\n\n**Why These Fit Your Preferences**\n- Oaked Chardonnays from these regions are specifically known for the hazelnut and creamy notes you enjoy.\n- Ontario options are local, fresher, and often better value in Canada.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific Ontario producers or tips on how to spot a hazelnut-forward Chardonnay on the label?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0022-04-12330:4": -0.01119593158364296, "clueweb22-en0022-04-12330:3": -0.019577838480472565, "clueweb22-en0034-95-07216:18": -0.03624381124973297, "clueweb22-en0034-95-07216:19": -0.04574212059378624, "clueweb22-en0035-82-12407:5": -0.045784369111061096}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I live in Ca