{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For combining yoga with outdoor swimming near London, here’s what you need to budget for the most accessible and popular spots:\n\n**Beckenham Place Park Swimming Lake (Lewisham, South-East London)**\n- **Swim Session:** £5–£5.50 per visit\n- **Induction (one-time, required):** £10\n- **Tow Float (required):** May need to purchase or rent (not included in session price)\n- **Booking:** Required in advance; sessions run most days, with good availability\n- **Concessions:** £3 per session available\n\n**Hampstead Heath Ponds (North London)**\n- **Swim Session:** £4 per visit (£2.40 concessions)\n- **Booking:** Some sessions are free-flow (no booking), others require advance booking\n- **Facilities:** Changing rooms available\n\n**West Reservoir Centre (Hackney)**\n- **Swim Session:** £10 for a 50-minute slot\n- **Booking:** Via Better UK app, required in advance\n\n**Additional Costs**\n- **Yoga:** Drop-in classes in London typically range from £10–£20 per session, or less with class packs/memberships.\n- **Equipment:** Swimsuit, towel, and possibly a tow float (for open water). Yoga mat if practicing outside a studio.\n\n**Summary:**  \nExpect to spend £4–£10 per swim, plus a one-time induction if required. Yoga costs are separate. Beckenham Place Park is a standout for its natural setting and moderate pricing, but Hampstead Heath Ponds are also affordable and centrally located.\n\nWould you like help finding yoga classes nearby, or tips on combining both activities into a weekly routine?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-06-14225:2": -0.005459517706185579, "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:2": -0.010073182173073292, "clueweb22-en0011-32-16579:10": -0.010113895870745182, "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:1": -0.010746464133262634, "clueweb22-en0012-69-04768:3": -0.01274158526211977}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I live in London, but my