{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For training in New York City before your race, you have excellent options tailored to different preferences:\n\n**Outdoor Running & Fitness:**\n- **Central Park:** Classic choice with varied terrain and scenic loops, ideal for all distances.\n- **Prospect Park (Brooklyn):** Quieter, with a 3.35-mile loop—great for focused runs.\n- **Hudson River Park:** Flat, riverside paths stretching from Battery Park up the west side—perfect for long runs with views.\n\n**Outdoor Yoga & Recovery:**\n- **Bryant Park:** Free outdoor yoga classes (Tuesdays and Thursdays, mats provided). Welcoming for all levels, set in a relaxing green space.\n- **Prospect Park:** Seasonal outdoor vinyasa yoga sessions on the Long Meadow, often with community vibes and post-class organic tea.\n\n**Top Gyms & Indoor Training:**\n- **Equinox Sports Club (Upper West Side):** Luxury facilities, outdoor track, pool, and a wide range of classes. Ideal if you want premium amenities and recovery options.\n- **Chelsea Piers Fitness:** Features an indoor running track, swimming pool, and outdoor sun decks. Great for cross-training or if weather is unpredictable.\n\n**Personalization:**  \nIf you prefer outdoor, social, and scenic workouts, Central Park, Prospect Park, and Bryant Park yoga are top picks. For structured training or bad weather, Equinox and Chelsea Piers offer everything you need.\n\nWould you like details on running routes, class schedules, or day passes for these gyms?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0043-06-14487:1": -0.013957628048956394, "clueweb22-en0016-04-02118:0": -0.014290140941739082, "clueweb22-en0043-06-14487:0": -0.01475763600319624, "clueweb22-en0008-95-04168:9": -0.020868495106697083, "clueweb22-en0005-09-18970:0": -0.02232852205634117}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I live in Spain.", "I am not very confident in my fitness level."]}], "