{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help you build healthier meals, focus on these core ingredient groups and strategies:\n\n**1. Essential Healthy Ingredients**\n- **Vegetables & Fruits:** Aim for at least 5 servings daily. They’re nutrient-dense, low-calorie, and packed with antioxidants, vitamins, and minerals.\n- **Whole Grains:** Choose brown rice, oats, whole grain breads, and pasta. These provide fiber, B vitamins, and help regulate digestion.\n- **Lean Proteins:** Include seafood (especially fatty fish like salmon or sardines 2–3 times/week), lean meats, eggs, legumes (beans, lentils), and low-fat dairy.\n- **Healthy Fats:** Prioritize olive oil, nuts, seeds, avocado, and oily fish. Limit saturated fats (found in full-fat dairy and fatty meats).\n- **Pulses:** Beans and lentils are excellent for fiber and plant-based protein—aim for 2 servings per week.\n\n**2. Smart Meal Planning Tips**\n- **Balance Macronutrients:** Each meal should have protein, healthy fats, and complex carbs.\n- **Plan Ahead:** Write out weekly menus and shopping lists to ensure you have healthy options on hand.\n- **Seasonal & Whole Foods:** Opt for seasonal produce and minimally processed foods for better nutrition and value.\n- **Limit Added Sugar & Refined Grains:** Replace white flour with whole grains and cut back on sugary foods and drinks.\n\n**3. Portion & Timing**\n- Distribute calories across 5 meals a day.\n- Eat fruit and carbs earlier in the day if you’re watching weight.\n\nWould you like a sample healthy meal plan or a shopping list to get started?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0013-86-01917:9": -0.08593063801527023, "clueweb22-en0029-30-05433:2": -0.08964714407920837, "clueweb22-en0001-08-01588:0": -0.12890417873859406, "clueweb22-en0007-79-17890:5": -0.13320384919643402, "clueweb22-en0029-30-05433:1": -0.15251986682415009}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I usu