{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For a healthier, low-carb, nutrient-rich breakfast that supports your calcium needs and still satisfies your taste for white bread and jam, here’s a targeted approach:\n\n**Best Bread Alternatives**\n- **Whole Grain or Sprouted Grain Bread:** Delivers more nutrients and fiber than white bread, with a texture closer to what you enjoy. Sprouted grain breads also have a lower impact on blood sugar.\n- **Almond or Coconut Flour Bread:** Lower in carbs, higher in protein and healthy fats. These options mimic the softness of white bread but are much more nutrient-dense.\n- **Lavash or Lettuce Wraps:** If you want to go ultra low-carb, these can replace bread entirely, but may not satisfy your craving for traditional bread texture.\n\n**Boosting Calcium & Protein**\n- **Greek Yogurt or Cottage Cheese:** Both are high in calcium and protein. Use them as a base for your jam instead of bread, or as a side.\n- **Toppings:** Add nuts (almonds, walnuts) or seeds (chia, flax, hemp) to yogurt or on top of bread for extra protein, healthy fats, and calcium.\n\n**Healthier Jam Choices**\n- **Chia Seed Jam:** Make your own by mixing chia seeds with mashed berries. This is lower in sugar, higher in fiber, and adds calcium.\n\n**Sample Breakfast**\n- Whole grain toast (or almond flour bread) topped with cottage cheese and a spoonful of chia seed jam, plus a sprinkle of nuts.\n\nWould you like quick recipes for these options or more ideas for low-carb, high-calcium breakfasts?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0015-58-07396:7": -0.04592135176062584, "clueweb22-en0011-98-07078:3": -0.08519688248634338, "clueweb22-en0015-58-07396:6": -0.10752672702074051, "clueweb22-en0032-09-07542:3": -0.10953254997730255, "clueweb22-en0027-52-18570:11": -0.12398479133844376}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I think I don't get enough calcium, and I am worried about i