{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For healthy, nutrient-dense lunch alternatives to white rice, here are the best options tailored to your goals (lower carbs, higher nutrients, and variety):\n\n**Top Rice Alternatives**\n\n- **Cauliflower Rice**\n  - ~25–27 kcal/100g, 5g carbs, 2g protein, 2g fiber\n  - Extremely low in calories and carbs\n  - High in vitamin C, folate, vitamin K\n  - Neutral flavor—pairs well with most dishes\n\n- **Broccoli Rice**\n  - Similar calories and nutrients to cauliflower rice\n  - Adds extra fiber, plant protein, and iron\n\n- **Shirataki Rice (\"Miracle Rice\")**\n  - ~1–3g carbs/serving, almost zero calories\n  - Made from konjac root; gluten-free, soy-free\n  - High in fiber, very filling\n\n- **Sweet Potato Rice**\n  - ~110 kcal/100g, 23g carbs, 5g fiber\n  - Higher in carbs but rich in vitamin C and fiber\n  - Slightly sweet, good for variety\n\n- **Quinoa**\n  - ~120 kcal/100g, higher protein and fiber than rice\n  - Not as low-carb, but more filling and nutritious\n\n- **Black Rice, Wild Rice, Brown Rice**\n  - ~110 kcal/100g, more protein, fiber, and antioxidants than white rice\n  - Black rice especially high in antioxidants\n\n**Personalization for You**\n- If you enjoy variety and want to keep lunch light (especially if you snack on cake with coffee), cauliflower or broccoli rice and shirataki rice are best for low calories and carbs.\n- For more substance or a heartier meal, quinoa or black rice are excellent, nutrient-rich choices.\n\nWould you like quick recipes or meal ideas using any of these alternatives?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0032-31-12698:1": -0.02082541584968567, "clueweb22-en0018-51-09385:1": -0.022611182183027267, "clueweb22-en0032-31-12698:0": -0.023651495575904846, "clueweb22-en0004-56-06690:4": -0.03159506246447563, "clueweb22-en0032-35-04029:9": -0.03474859520792961}, "ptkb_provenance":