{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Congratulations again! Here’s what you need to know about diet changes in pregnancy, tailored to your habits:\n\n**You don’t need to “eat for two.”** Focus on quality, not quantity. A balanced, varied diet is key.\n\n**Fruit & Vegetables:**  \n- Aim for at least 5 portions daily (fresh, frozen, canned, dried, or juiced).  \n- Wash all produce well.  \n- Your afternoon fresh orange juice is great—just avoid street-sold or preservative-heavy juices. Eating whole oranges is even better for fiber and nutrients.\n\n**Breakfast (Jam):**  \n- Jam is fine in moderation, but try to pair it with wholegrain bread for more fiber and longer-lasting energy.\n\n**Lunch (White Rice):**  \n- White rice is okay, but consider swapping in brown rice or mixing with other grains sometimes for extra fiber and nutrients.\n\n**Snacks (Cake & Coffee):**  \n- Cakes are best as an occasional treat. Try to balance with healthier snacks like fruit, low-fat yogurt, or nuts to avoid too much sugar and saturated fat.\n\n**General Tips:**  \n- No need to cut out your favorites—just balance them with more fruits, veggies, and whole grains.  \n- Drink plenty of water.  \n- Swap sugary drinks for water or healthy alternatives when possible.\n\nWould you like specific meal or snack ideas that fit your preferences and support a healthy pregnancy?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-84-16614:12": -0.06885775923728943, "clueweb22-en0000-84-16614:3": -0.10323335230350494, "clueweb22-en0000-84-16614:2": -0.11270029842853546, "clueweb22-en0027-89-15500:1": -0.22027403116226196, "clueweb22-en0028-58-13598:12": -0.23158806562423706}, "ptkb_provenance": ["Sometimes I drink fresh orange juice in the afternoon.", "I usually eat white rice for my lunch.", "I eat jam for breakfast.", "I like eating cake as a snack with coffee, and I bake cakes every week."]}], "refe