{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, your routine must be adjusted to protect your sensitized skin and maximize results—especially given your current use of vitamin C, retinol, and AHA/BHA.\n\n**What to Do After Microneedling:**\n- **Gentle Cleansing:** Use only a mild, fragrance-free cleanser for several days. Avoid harsh scrubbing or cleansing brushes.\n- **Hydration:** Continue using hyaluronic acid serum—this is ideal for post-microneedling as it hydrates and supports healing.\n- **Moisturize:** Opt for gentle, non-comedogenic moisturizers with ceramides or peptides.\n- **Sun Protection:** Apply a physical (mineral) sunscreen daily, as your skin will be more sun-sensitive.\n\n**What to Avoid (Crucial for Your Routine):**\n- **No Vitamin C, Retinol, or AHA/BHA:** Stop using these actives for at least 5–7 days post-treatment, or until all redness and irritation have subsided. These ingredients can cause irritation and delay healing on freshly microneedled skin.\n- **No Makeup:** Avoid makeup for at least 24 hours, ideally 48, to prevent irritation and infection.\n- **No Exfoliation:** Skip scrubs, peels, or any exfoliating tools for at least a week.\n\n**When to Resume Your Routine:**\n- Once your skin is fully healed (usually after 5–7 days), you can gradually reintroduce vitamin C, retinol, and AHA/BHA—one at a time, monitoring for any sensitivity.\n\nWould you like a step-by-step sample routine for the first week post-microneedling?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:3": -0.027718713507056236, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:17": -0.046073682606220245, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:6": -0.06365864723920822, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:16": -0.08249163627624512, "clueweb22-en0008-38-11917:8": -0.08911372721195221}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning rou