{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You asked if you can continue using your salicylic acid face wash after microneedling, given your oily skin and scalp.\n\n**Direct Answer:**  \nIt’s best to pause your salicylic acid face wash for at least 3 days after microneedling.\n\n**Key Points:**\n\n- **Why Pause?**  \n  Salicylic acid (a beta hydroxy acid) can irritate freshly microneedled skin, slow healing, and increase dryness or sensitivity. This is true even for oily skin types.\n\n- **When to Resume?**  \n  Most dermatology sources recommend waiting 3–7 days post-treatment before reintroducing salicylic acid or any exfoliating acids. Let your skin fully recover first.\n\n- **What to Use Instead?**  \n  Stick to gentle, hydrating products—especially hyaluronic acid and a mild, non-foaming cleanser. Avoid anything with acids, retinoids, or strong actives during the first week.\n\n- **Oily Scalp/Hair:**  \n  Microneedling for the face doesn’t affect your scalp routine. You can continue your usual hair care unless your scalp was also treated.\n\n**Personalized Justification:**  \nBecause you have oily skin, salicylic acid is usually helpful—but after microneedling, your skin’s barrier is temporarily compromised and more prone to irritation. Giving it a break ensures optimal healing and results.\n\nWould you like recommendations for gentle cleansers or hydrating products to use during your recovery week?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": -0.02945217490196228, "clueweb22-en0030-56-13743:9": -0.13361039757728577, "clueweb22-en0000-59-08693:0": -0.14958405494689941, "clueweb22-en0030-56-13743:6": -0.16590680181980133, "clueweb22-en0002-91-08989:13": -0.1806063950061798}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning routine.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with 