{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For fatty liver, the healthiest homemade bread options are:\n\n**Top Recommendation: Rye + Whole Wheat Bread**\n- Mixing rye flour with whole wheat flour creates a bread that’s high in fiber, digests slowly, and is much better for liver health than white bread.\n- Pure rye bread is even healthier but can be dense and bitter; blending with whole wheat improves taste and texture.\n- Avoid store-bought rye: many contain added sugars and white flour. Baking at home lets you control ingredients.\n\n**Other Good Options**\n- **Sprouted Grain Bread**: Made from sprouted whole grains (like Ezekiel bread), it’s nutrient-rich and has a lower impact on blood sugar. Baking at home is challenging, but it’s a strong choice if you’re up for it.\n- **Whole Wheat Bread**: If you prefer a familiar taste, 100% whole wheat bread is much better than white bread. Look for recipes with just flour, yeast, salt, and water.\n\n**What to Avoid**\n- White bread and most commercial breads (even “healthy” ones) often contain added sugars, preservatives, and refined flours that can worsen fatty liver.\n\n**Portion Guidance**\n- Even with healthy bread, limit yourself to 2–3 slices per day to support liver recovery.\n\nWould you like a simple recipe for homemade rye/whole wheat bread, or tips on making it lighter and tastier?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:10": -0.006159134209156036, "clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:11": -0.007852044887840748, "clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:2": -0.00828827265650034, "clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:1": -0.013793975114822388, "clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:7": -0.016647355630993843}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I enjoy baking.", "I have some basic baking experience."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:10": -0.006159134209156036, "clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:11": -0.007852044887840748, "clueweb22-en0046-25-14652:2": -0