{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Since you already have a scale and measuring cups, here are the most useful additional tools for healthy, oven-baked bread at home:\n\n**Must-Have Tools:**\n- **Large Mixing Bowl:** Essential for mixing and proofing dough.\n- **Dutch Oven or Baking Stone:** Either helps create a crisp crust and even bake. A Dutch oven traps steam for a better rise; a baking stone gives a classic, rustic bottom crust.\n- **Bread Thermometer:** Ensures your bread is fully baked (look for an internal temp of ~200°F/93°C).\n- **Bench/Dough Scraper:** Makes handling, dividing, and cleaning up dough much easier.\n- **Cooling Rack:** Prevents sogginess by allowing air to circulate around your bread as it cools.\n\n**Nice-to-Have:**\n- **Scoring Lame (or sharp knife):** For slashing the dough before baking, which controls expansion and gives a professional look.\n- **Oven Thermometer:** Confirms your oven is at the right temperature, crucial for consistent results.\n- **Bowl Scraper:** Helps get every bit of dough out of your mixing bowl.\n\n**Why these?**  \nThey directly support healthy, whole-grain bread baking by improving dough handling, bake quality, and consistency—important for your fatty liver-friendly recipes.\n\nWould you like tips on where to find these tools, or guidance on using them for your first loaf?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0046-36-14913:3": -0.009845269843935966, "clueweb22-en0012-81-07051:18": -0.01003872137516737, "clueweb22-en0022-71-14456:4": -0.011308031156659126, "clueweb22-en0038-14-07636:2": -0.011354116722941399, "clueweb22-en0020-01-06267:3": -0.011469852179288864}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I enjoy baking.", "I have some basic baking experience."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0046-36-14913:3": -0.009845269843935966, "clueweb22-en0012-81-07051:18": -0.01003872137516737, "clueweb22-en0022-71-14456:4": -0.011