{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Managing ADHD at work—especially in an office environment—requires targeted strategies to address distractibility, organization, and time management. Here’s a distilled, office-specific action plan tailored for you:\n\n**Minimize Distractions**\n- Use noise-cancelling headphones or play white noise/classical music to block out office sounds.\n- If possible, request a quieter workspace (private office, quiet cubicle) or use unused meeting rooms for focused tasks.\n- Route calls to voicemail and check them at set times to avoid interruptions.\n\n**Stay Organized**\n- Keep your workspace clutter-free; assign specific spots for essential items.\n- Use a notepad or digital tool to jot down ideas and reminders as they come—this helps manage forgetfulness and keeps you on task.\n- Maintain to-do lists and check them regularly to combat daydreaming and procrastination.\n\n**Manage Time and Tasks**\n- Avoid over-scheduling; break large projects into smaller, manageable steps.\n- Set clear priorities each day and use reminders or alarms to stay on track.\n- Limit access to distracting websites or social media during work hours.\n\n**Communication & Support**\n- If you struggle with communication or complex projects, consider seeking guidance from a career counselor or workplace coach familiar with ADHD.\n- Let trusted colleagues or supervisors know about your needs if you’re comfortable—they may help accommodate your working style.\n\nWould you like practical tools (apps, planners) or advice on discussing accommodations with your employer in Germany?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": -0.008144027553498745, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:0": -0.009128738194704056, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": -0.009572438895702362, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": -0.010114132426679134, "clueweb22-en0017-60-15663:0": -0.01269285567