{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To get started applying ink as a self-taught hobbyist, you already have the essentials: a tattoo machine and fake skin. Here’s what else you’ll need, with a focus on safe, effective practice and leveraging your drawing skills:\n\n**Core Supplies**\n- **Sterile Needles:** Multiple sizes for lining and shading. Pre-sterilized, single-use only.\n- **Tattoo Inks:** Start with a few reputable, skin-safe colors. (Some kits offer a wide range, but quality matters more than quantity.)\n- **Power Supply & Foot Pedal:** Reliable, adjustable voltage for consistent results.\n- **Grips, Tips, and Tubes:** For comfort and control; match to your needle types.\n- **Ink Cups & Holders:** For organizing and safely dispensing ink.\n\n**Hygiene & Safety**\n- **Disposable Gloves:** Always wear during setup, tattooing, and cleanup.\n- **Antibacterial Soap & Disinfectants:** For cleaning your workspace and equipment.\n- **Sharps Container:** For safe needle disposal.\n- **Antiseptic Wipes & Skin Cleansers:** For prepping practice skin and, eventually, real skin.\n- **Cleaning Brushes & Adjustment Tools:** For machine maintenance.\n\n**Practice Tools**\n- **Transfer Paper & Marking Pens:** To transfer your designs onto fake skin, maximizing your drawing ability.\n- **Extra Practice Skin:** Allows you to experiment and refine technique without risk.\n\n**Why This Matters for You**\n- Your drawing skills will shine if you use transfer paper to replicate your art precisely.\n- Prioritize hygiene—even on fake skin—to build safe habits from the start.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific brands or a step-by-step beginner practice routine?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0020-24-16033:20": -0.013440714217722416, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:15": -0.018293356522917747, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:17": -0.018839823082089424, "clueweb22-en002