{"metadata": {"team_id": "grilllab", "run_id": "grilllab-larf-finetuned", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The best resource for learning about REACH and safe tattooing in Germany is the official website of the European Chemicals Agency (ECHA), which provides clear, up-to-date information on the REACH regulation and its impact on tattoo inks and supplies.\n\n**Why ECHA?**\n- **Authoritative & Up-to-date:** ECHA is responsible for drafting and updating REACH regulations, so their site offers the most accurate and current guidance.\n- **Practical Guidance:** They explain which chemicals are restricted, why, and what to look for in compliant products.\n- **Health & Safety Focus:** ECHA details the risks associated with non-compliant inks (e.g., allergies, genetic mutations, cancer), helping you understand why compliance matters—even for hobbyists.\n\n**How to Use It:**\n- Visit [ECHA’s Tattoo Inks & Permanent Make-up page](https://echa.europa.eu/hot-topics/tattoo-inks).\n- Look for sections on “What is REACH?” and “What does it mean for tattooing?”\n- Check their lists of restricted substances and tips for choosing safe products.\n\n**For Hobbyists in Germany:**\n- Stick to REACH-compliant inks and needles, even for fake skin, to build safe habits.\n- Many reputable European tattoo supply shops (like Killer Ink) highlight REACH compliance in product descriptions.\n\nIf you want a more hands-on learning resource, consider online tattoo hygiene courses from reputable European providers—they often include REACH basics.\n\nWould you like recommendations for specific online courses or tutorials that cover both technique and safety?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-89-03397:1": -0.02303880639374256, "clueweb22-en0033-74-18753:1": -0.02303880639374256, "clueweb22-en0000-83-16967:1": -0.02908448688685894, "clueweb22-en0000-83-16967:2": -0.03527889773249626, "clueweb22-en0011-39-07888:1": -0.03599568456411362}, "ptkb_provenance":